  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1219 AM CST Tue Nov 24 2026\n\nWe will see a secondary front push through on Tuesday, ensuring a \nchilly Thanksgiving across the area. Isolated to scattered showers \nwill be expected thanks to some weak isentropic lift at the 305K \nlevel. There will be a weak shortwave passing through that could \nhelp assist the activity. The caveat will will be there is drier air \nin the lower levels that will work against this. The likely outcome \nwill remain light rain and drizzle with some areas with mixed in \nsteadier rainfall. This front will give us a reinforcing surge of \ncooler air as high pressure builds in behind it. High temperatures \nwill be in the upper 50s to low 60s through the remainder of the \nweek! Lows on tonight through Thursday night will be very cold with \nlows in the 30s across the area. We could see some wind chill values \ndip into the upper 20s in the northern portions of the CWA. \n\n\nWe will see onshore flow returning to the region by the end of the \nweek. This will allow for us to finally begin warming back up into \nthe 70s.",
